{{!
    @template block_dimensions/page

    The block's content on its own page: the summary template as a partial, fed the same
    context, inside a wrapper carrying block_dimensions - the class core puts on the block's
    section and the one styles.css scopes every rule to - but not core's block card chrome,
    which needs a block instance behind it. dims-page is the page's own hook for selectors.

    Context variables required for this template: those of block_dimensions/summary.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "containerid": "block_dimensions_1",
        "showheading": true,
        "showsearch": true,
        "showsectionheaders": true,
        "endpointmethod": "block_dimensions_get_block_dataset",
        "filtersettingsjson": "{}",
        "favouritesenabled": true,
        "labelsjson": "{}",
        "isbs4": false
    }
}}
<div class="block_dimensions dims-page">
    {{> block_dimensions/summary }}
</div>
